# Network and API

HTTP access against `hms-backend` per [`.cursor/api-contract.mdc`](../../.cursor/api-contract.mdc).

## Mandatory rules

- Repository contracts must live in the domain layer; no HTTP from UI.
- Must use `dio` for clients and interceptors.
- DTOs must live in the data layer with `snake_case` JSON mapping.
- Must map API errors to app failures before UI.
- Must apply request timeouts and support cancellation for stale requests.
- Must not log tokens, passwords, or sensitive payloads.
- Must handle `401` through the session manager.
- Base URLs and timeouts must be environment-driven.
- HTTP owns CRUD mutations; WebSocket listeners refresh UI after server broadcasts ([`realtime_sync.mdc`](./realtime_sync.mdc)).
- DTOs and API paths exposed to presentation must use `human_friendly_id` (or domain aliases like `displayId`); must not surface raw database primary keys.
- Repositories map `human_friendly_id` on the wire; internal IDs stay in the data/backend layer only.

## Client layout

```txt
core/network/
├── api_client.dart
├── api_endpoints.dart
├── api_interceptors.dart
├── api_result.dart
└── network_failure_mapper.dart
```

